# {{.Name}}

A static website made with [Hydrogen](https://github.com/hydrogencms/hydrogen). The content lives in git, editors
work in the admin, and GitHub Pages serves the result.

```
content/              the content, committed (a `hydrogen export`): the source of truth
schema/               page and block types (types.yaml, blocks.yaml)
config/               server, database and the one web channel
site/                 the Astro site: templates, block components, styles
.github/workflows/    builds the site from content/ and deploys it to GitHub Pages
```

## Run it

You need Go 1.26 and Node 22.12 or later.

```sh
hydrogen dev                      # the CMS on http://127.0.0.1:8080; loads content/ into .work/hydrogen.db
cd site && npm install && npm run dev      # the site on http://localhost:4321
```

`hydrogen dev` prints a link that creates the first administrator. Open it, choose a password, and edit pages in the
admin (http://127.0.0.1:8080/admin). Preview shows drafts of the page you edit while `npm run dev` runs; publish a
page, then reload the site. `hydrogen dev` also regenerates `gen/` (typed code, the site imports its TypeScript types)
when the schema changes.

Preview works only in `npm run dev`: there `site/src/pages/[...path].astro` and `404.astro` render on demand (the
integration's `devRoutes` option lists more, if you add page routes). `npm run build` stays fully static. Share links
are off (`delivery.share_links` in `config/app.yaml`) because they would point at the local dev server.
{{if .Core}}
The `@hydrogencms/*` packages in `site/package.json` are `file:` dependencies on your hydrogen checkout; build its
`packages/` first (`npm run build` there).
{{end}}
## Edit, save, publish

1. Edit and publish in the admin. Your edits live in the local database in `.work/`, which is not committed.
2. Write them to the repository: `hydrogen content:save`. It updates `content/`; review it with `git diff content`.
3. `git add content && git commit && git push`. The workflow builds and deploys the site.

After a `git pull` that changes `content/`, restart `hydrogen dev`: the start loads the new content (the old database
is moved to `.work/backups/`). If you edited and your teammates changed `content/` too, the start asks you to choose:
`hydrogen content:save` keeps your edits, `hydrogen content:load -force` keeps the directory. Users are not part of
the content, so loading a changed directory resets them; the first-run link creates the administrator again. See
[content in git](https://hydrogencms.github.io/website/docs/content-in-git/).

## Deploy to GitHub Pages

1. Create a repository, then `git init`, commit everything (including `site/package-lock.json`, created by
   `npm install`) and push to `main`.
2. In the repository, open Settings > Pages and set Source to **GitHub Actions**.
3. Every push to `main` runs `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`: it builds the CMS from this repository, starts it (it loads
   `content/` into a fresh SQLite database), builds `site/` against it and deploys `site/dist`.

For a project site (`https://you.github.io/repo/`) the workflow passes the origin in `SITE_URL` and the base path in
`SITE_BASE` (`/repo`; empty for a custom domain or a `you.github.io` site). The Astro config reads both and the
channel reads `SITE_URL`. Locally you can build the same way:

```sh
SITE_URL=https://you.github.io SITE_BASE=/repo npm run build     # in site/, with the CMS running
npm run preview
```

The workflow starts the CMS as `APP_ENV=production` with a secret made for the run, because it needs no dev defaults and
production fails early on a missing secret. A custom domain needs no change: Pages reports it as the site's address.

## Change the site

- **New block**: add it to `schema/blocks.yaml` and to `allow` in `schema/types.yaml`, run `hydrogen generate` (or
  keep `hydrogen dev` running), write `site/src/components/blocks/<Name>.astro` and add it to
  `site/src/components/registry.ts`.
- **New page type**: add the type to `schema/types.yaml` (`page: true` puts it in the page tree), then add a template in
  `site/src/templates/`, and list the type in `templates` in `site/src/hydrogen.ts` and in `[...path].astro`.
- **Links** in blocks pick a page (`ref`) or hold a URL; `site/src/lib/link.ts` turns them into paths with the base.

Changing the schema can make the committed content invalid; the start of `hydrogen dev` says what is wrong. Fields that
change shape need a content migration, see [schema](https://hydrogencms.github.io/website/docs/schema/).
